      "writtenOn": "2024-09-19T23:13:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO, if we want to serialize access to the fields of `AudioCommand` properly, we should add thread safety annotations:\n\n```\n        class AudioCommand: public RefBase {\n...\n            mutable audio_utils::mutex mMutex{audio_utils::MutexOrder::kAudioCommand_Mutex};\n            mutable audio_utils::condition_variable mCond; // condition for status return\n            status_t mStatus GUARDED_BY(mMutex); // command status\n            bool mWaitStatus GUARDED_BY(mMutex); // true if caller is waiting for status\n...\n        };\n\n```\n\nalso, make immutable fields `const`, and then address all compiler complaints about non thread-safe access. Otherwise, it\u0027s just a half-measure which creates an illusion of thread safety, while still remaining prone to races.",
      "range": {
